    "profile": {
      "items": [
        {
          "type": "HTML",
          "html": "Picked to play his first Test in his hometown of Calcutta in\nhis 30th year, `Montu' Banerjee, a brisk right arm medium pacer\nrelished the familiar conditions and took four for 120 and one\nfor 61, bowling 51 overs in all. In his first spell he dismissed\nAllan Rae for 15 and D.Atkinson for zero. In a later spell he got\nthe wickets of Christiani and Cameron. In the second innings also\nhe struck early removing Carew. He also held a couple of catches\nto complete an impressive debut and it was rather surprising that\nhe never got another chance at the international level. In a\nfirst class career that lasted from 1941 to 1954, Banerjee\ntook 92 wickets (23.28).(<b><i>Partab Ramchand</i></b>)"
        }
      ]
    },
